{"id": 36, "ts": 1780428995.613419, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m in line with the early inclination toward Candidate\u202fB. From my notes, B is very conscientious \u2013 a clear indicator of operational reliability \u2013 and handles stress exceptionally well, which is vital for long\u2011distance routes. Their ability to assess weather conditions and strong computer skills speak to the technical and cognitive competence we need. The only red flags are the reports of occasional grumpiness and a tendency to be uncooperative, which could affect crew cooperation and professional communication. Compared with Candidate\u202fC, who is 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere but has notable communication difficulties and limited willingness to further his education, B\u2019s stress resilience and technical aptitude give him a stronger overall safety profile for this role. I therefore keep my vote for Candidate\u202fB, while recommending we explore the cooperation concern further in any follow\u2011up."}
